        "original_id": "e2b282b1-6d80-5d8b-9e18-48af648f09c8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: Royal Oak Mines, Northgate Minerals\n- Places: Kemess Mine, Colomac Mine, Kemess Creek Airport, British Columbia, Northwest Territories, Yellowknife, Canada\n- Topics: mine ownership and operation, airport location\n\nFacts:\n- In 1994, the Colomac Mine reopened under Royal Oak Mines Inc.\n- From 1998 to 1999, Royal Oak Mines operated the Kemess Mine.\n- In 1999, Northgate Minerals bought the Kemess Mine.\n- The Colomac Mine was a privately owned and operated open pit gold mine located 220 km northwest of Yellowknife in the Northwest Territories, Canada.\n- Kemess Creek Airport, with TC LID CBQ7, is located near Kemess Mine in British Columbia, Canada.",
